; All three are `invalid_manifest` — the manifest itself is wrong, and
; that is the code the loader already uses for `(member-set …)`'s
; equivalent rejections. A fourth condition, a count that is negative /
; fractional / over `u16`, reports `wrong_underlying` instead: it reuses
; the same out-of-range check `(fixed N)` and `(range :min …)` go
; through, and the condition is identical.
;
; Three reports, not one: the loader keeps going after a bad head-set
; rather than abandoning the manifest at the first, so all three
; conditions surface in one pass.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :severity err :path [mixed heads])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :severity err :path [duplicated heads])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :severity err :path [backwards heads vertex]))
